# Fresh simulator storage opens the first Easy puzzle.
wait-for-id game-more
expect Sudoku · Easy 1
expect Choose a square · 53 left
# Undo is first at the foot, and says so when there is nothing to undo.
tap-id game-undo
wait-idle
expect Nothing to undo yet.
# With no square chosen, Erase and Reveal say what they need.
tap-id erase
expect Choose a square to erase.
tap-id game-more
tap-id hint
expect Choose a square to reveal.
tap-id cell-0
tap-id pencil
tap-id digit-2
wait-idle
expect Notes
shot sudoku-notes
# Notes sit in a ninth of their square each, and an entered digit is grey
# beside the printed ones.
tap-id digit-3
tap-id digit-7
tap-id pencil
tap-id cell-1
tap-id digit-6
expect 52 left
tap-id cell-3
wait-idle
shot sudoku-entries
# A printed number cannot be changed, erased or revealed.
tap-id cell-2
expect 52 left · Given
tap-id digit-5
expect 52 left · Given
tap-id erase
expect Given numbers cannot change.
tap-id game-more
tap-id hint
expect Given numbers cannot change.
# Notes cannot go over an answer until it is erased.
tap-id cell-1
tap-id pencil
tap-id digit-4
expect Erase this answer to add notes.
tap-id pencil
tap-id erase
expect 53 left
tap-id game-undo
expect 52 left
tap-id game-undo
tap-id game-undo
tap-id game-undo
tap-id game-undo
# Rules are one tap away in the top bar and run over more than one page.
tap-id game-rules
expect Use 1–9 once
expect-missing original puzzles at each difficulty
shot sudoku-help
tap Next
expect original puzzles at each difficulty
expect-missing Use 1–9 once
clean
shot sudoku-help-2
tap Previous
expect Use 1–9 once
tap Back
wait-idle
expect Sudoku · Easy 1
# More opens over the board: New game first, mistakes in plain words.
tap-id game-more
wait-idle
expect New game
expect Restart puzzle
expect Show mistakes
expect Reveal square
expect Use landscape
expect-missing Check off
expect-missing Retry saving
shot sudoku-more
tap-id checking
# The first square of Easy 1 is a 1, so a 2 is flagged in words and kept.
tap-id cell-0
tap-id digit-2
wait-idle
expect Wrong answer
tap-id game-undo
tap-id game-more
wait-idle
expect Hide mistakes
tap-id checking
tap-id erase
wait-idle
expect This square is already empty.
# Reveal asks first, Keep playing leaves the square, and a revealed square is right.
tap-id cell-3
tap-id game-more
tap-id hint
expect Reveal square?
expect count one hint
clean
shot sudoku-reveal-confirm
tap Keep playing
expect 53 left
tap-id game-more
tap-id hint
tap-id confirm-hint
expect 52 left
tap-id game-more
tap-id hint
expect This square is already right.
# Restart asks first, clears the board, and can be undone.
tap-id game-more
tap-id restart
expect Restart puzzle?
expect Clear answers, notes and hints. You can undo.
clean
shot sudoku-restart-confirm
tap Keep playing
expect 52 left
tap-id game-more
tap-id restart
tap-id confirm-restart
expect 53 left
tap-id game-undo
expect 52 left
# New game warns that it replaces a game in progress, and Keep playing keeps it.
tap-id game-more
tap-id game-new
expect Replaces this game and its history.
expect Easy
expect Medium
expect Hard
clean
shot sudoku-new-game-warning
tap Keep playing
expect Sudoku · Easy 1
expect 52 left
# A failed save is named in the status line and Retry saving joins More.
scenario storage-full
tap-id cell-7
tap-id digit-3
wait-idle
expect Not saved · Retry saving in More.
tap-id game-more
expect Retry saving
clean
shot sudoku-save-refused
scenario normal
tap-id retry-save
wait-idle
expect-missing Not saved
tap-id game-more
expect-missing Retry saving
tap-id game-more
# Reopening keeps the board and the undo history.
restart
wait-for Sudoku · Easy 1
expect 51 left
tap-id game-undo
expect 52 left
clean
shot sudoku-resumed
# Each difficulty deals its own first puzzle.
tap-id game-more
tap-id game-new
tap-id new-medium
wait-idle
expect Sudoku · Medium 1
clean
shot sudoku-medium
tap-id game-more
tap-id game-new
expect Choose a difficulty.
tap-id new-hard
wait-idle
expect Sudoku · Hard 1
clean
shot sudoku-hard
tap-id game-more
tap-id game-new
tap-id new-easy
wait-idle
expect Sudoku · Easy 2
shot sudoku-game
